{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>For he was good, and she hid him, etc.</b> One must examine what the goodness was that she saw in him. And our Sages of blessed memory (Sotah 12a) said: he was born circumcised, and the house was filled with light. And this is the way of derash. Further, one must examine the connection of ״וַתִּצְפְּנֵהוּ״ with ״וַתֵּרֶא אוֹתוֹ כִּי טוֹב״ etc. — for if he had not been good, would she not have had compassion on the fruit of her womb to hide him from men of blood?" "<b>Indeed,</b> the intent of the verse is this: from the fact that the verse says ״וַתִּצְפְּנֵהוּ״ etc. ״וְלֹא יָכְלָה עוֹד״ etc., our Sages of blessed memory (Sotah 12a) said that the Egyptians counted for her from the time of her pregnancy, and she gave birth to him at six months and one day. Now, one born at six months is plainly not viable, while one born at seven months is viable; and a woman does not reckon precisely by a single day, so that when she gave birth to him he was in the presumption of being a stillborn (nephel). And the verse informed us that she saw him good — meaning, healthy and strong, bearing no signs of a nephel — and therefore she exerted herself on his behalf and endangered herself from the Egyptians, who would inspect the houses for infants, as our Sages of blessed memory stated there (ibid.); and this is what it means by <b>וַתֵּרֶא</b> etc. <b>וַתִּצְפְּנֵהוּ.</b> And the derash of our Sages of blessed memory is derived from the fact that it chose this expression <b>כִּי טוֹב</b> and did not use another expression. And the intent of our Sages of blessed memory when they interpreted ״טוֹב הוּא״ as מָהוּל (circumcised) — they had already revealed their view in another place (Sanhedrin 38b), that Adam the first man, before he sinned, was absolute good, and through the evil deed he did, he drew the foreskin (orlah) from the side of evil. Therefore, when the verse says ״כִּי טוֹב,״ this points clearly that he was free of the evil aspect, which is the orlah."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:23:34.993016707Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}